# Chat UI

Chat is a core learning feature.

## Message types

Depending on backend support:
- text
- image/media
- voice/audio
- correction
- reaction
- translation/AI suggestion

Do not assume a message type exists unless the API supports it.

## Message rendering

Message components should handle:
- sending
- sent
- delivered
- read
- failed
- retrying
- edited if supported

Never hide failed messages silently.

## Composer

The composer should support the backend's actual capabilities without becoming overloaded.

Keep primary actions obvious:
- text input
- send
- attachment/voice where supported

## Corrections

Corrections should visually distinguish:
- original learner message
- correction
- correction author
- optional explanation

Never visually imply that the original message was replaced.

## Realtime

Handle:
- incoming messages
- typing
- presence
- read receipts
- connection/reconnection

Use optimistic UI carefully.
A failed optimistic message must be recoverable.

## Pagination

Load older messages incrementally.
Do not fetch the entire conversation history at once.

Preserve scroll position when prepending older messages.
